{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Hear my voice, wives of Lemech.</b> He cries out in anguish." "<b>My saying.</b> That I shall recount my distress." "<b>I have slain for my wound.</b> I was wounded in my very self, in that the slain man was my father; <b>and a youth for my bruise</b> — the bruise was in my very self, in that the slain one was my son."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {2 "Sforno reads לפצעי and לחבורתי as referring to wounds Lemech suffered in his own person, identified through the kinship of the slain."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:29:07.857883929Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}